<h1 data-source-line="1">Math and Diagrams</h1>
<p data-source-line="3">KaTeX and Mermaid, rendered on the client from the source Arto keeps in the
page. Previous: <span data-md-link="./02-blocks.md" class="md-link" onmousedown="if(event.button===0||event.button===1){event.preventDefault();window.handleMarkdownLinkClick(this.dataset.mdLink,event.button)}">Block syntax</span>.</p>
<h2 data-source-line="6">Inline math</h2>
<p data-source-line="8">When <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="a \ne 0">a \ne 0</span>, the equation <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="ax^2 + bx + c = 0">ax^2 + bx + c = 0</span> has the solutions
<span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}">x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}</span>. Euler: <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0">e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0</span>.</p>
<p data-source-line="11"><strong>Expected:</strong> four typeset formulas flowing with the text.</p>
<h3 data-source-line="13">Math that contains Markdown punctuation</h3>
<p data-source-line="15">Asterisks: <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="2*3*4 = 24">2*3*4 = 24</span>. Underscores: <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="a_1 + b_2 = c_3">a_1 + b_2 = c_3</span>. Tildes:
<span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="x \sim \mathcal{N}(0, 1)">x \sim \mathcal{N}(0, 1)</span>. Brackets: <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="[a, b] \times (c, d)">[a, b] \times (c, d)</span>. Backslashes:
<span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="\{x \mid x &gt; 0\}">\{x \mid x &gt; 0\}</span>.</p>
<p data-source-line="19"><strong>Expected:</strong> five typeset formulas; no italics, no strikethrough, and no
links appear because of the punctuation inside the dollars.</p>
<h3 data-source-line="22">Math inside other inline syntax</h3>
<p data-source-line="24">Emphasized: <em>the identity <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="E = mc^2">E = mc^2</span> holds</em>. In a link: <span data-md-link="./README.md" class="md-link" onmousedown="if(event.button===0||event.button===1){event.preventDefault();window.handleMarkdownLinkClick(this.dataset.mdLink,event.button)}">see <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="\pi">\pi</span></span>.
Bold: <strong><span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="\alpha + \beta">\alpha + \beta</span></strong>.</p>
<p data-source-line="27"><strong>Expected:</strong> the formulas typeset inside the italic, link, and bold runs.</p>
<h3 data-source-line="29">Not math</h3>
<p data-source-line="31">Prices: costs $5 and $6, or $5.00 and <span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="6.50. Escaped: \$100 and \$200. Code:
`">6.50. Escaped: \$100 and \$200. Code:
`</span>HOME<code>and</code>$PATH`. A lone dollar sign $ in a sentence.</p>
<p data-source-line="34"><strong>Expected:</strong> every dollar sign stays visible as text; nothing is typeset.</p>
<h3 data-source-line="36">Math in table cells</h3>
<table data-source-line="38" data-source-line-end="41"><thead><tr><th>Formula</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr data-source-line="40"><td><span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="E = mc^2">E = mc^2</span></td><td>mass-energy</td></tr>
<tr data-source-line="41"><td><span class="preprocessed-math-inline" data-original-content="\sum_{i=1}^{n} i">\sum_{i=1}^{n} i</span></td><td>a sum</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p data-source-line="43"><strong>Expected:</strong> depends on the engine. See the Math in table cells section of
<span data-md-link="./05-beyond-gfm.md" class="md-link" onmousedown="if(event.button===0||event.button===1){event.preventDefault();window.handleMarkdownLinkClick(this.dataset.mdLink,event.button)}">Beyond GFM</span>.</p>
<h2 data-source-line="46">Display math</h2>
<p data-source-line="48">Double dollars on their own lines:</p>
<p data-source-line="50"><div data-source-line="50" data-source-line-end="52" class="preprocessed-math-display" data-original-content="
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi}
">
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi}
</div></p>
